.TH SPRACH 1 "2026-05-18" "sprachspiel 0.43.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sprach \- A powerful CLI for interacting with LLM models via Ollama and compatible backends
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sprach
.RI [ GLOBAL_OPTIONS ] " [ QUERY ]
.br
.B sprach
.RI [ GLOBAL_OPTIONS ] " query " [ QUERY ]
.br
.B sprach
.RI [ GLOBAL_OPTIONS ] " chat " [ CHAT_OPTIONS ]
.br
.B sprach
.RI [ GLOBAL_OPTIONS ] " translate " LANGUAGE [ TEXT ]
.br
.B sprach
.RI [ GLOBAL_OPTIONS ] " ocr " FILE ...
.br
.B sprach
.RI [ GLOBAL_OPTIONS ] " vision " FILE ...
.br
.B sprach
.RI [ GLOBAL_OPTIONS ] " summarize " [ TEXT ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sprach
is a Rust CLI tool for interacting with local and cloud LLM models (via Ollama and compatible backends), featuring markdown rendering, tool-assisted queries, translation, OCR, vision, and text summarization.
.PP
When invoked without a subcommand, it defaults to query mode. The application reads from stdin if no QUERY or TEXT is provided, making it suitable for piping.
.PP
If an AGENTS.md file exists in the current directory, it is automatically loaded and injected into the system prompt to provide project-specific context.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B query, q
Execute a query with the default or specified model. This is the default mode when no subcommand is given.
.TP
.B chat, c
Start interactive chat session with persistent conversation history. Conversations are saved per project. Documents and notes are rendered as markdown at 80 columns.
.TP
.B translate, t
Translate text between 50+ languages using TranslateGemma model.
.TP
.B ocr, o
Extract text from images using GLM-OCR. Supports text, tables, figures, and formulas.
.TP
.B vision, v
Analyze and describe images using vision models (moondream default). Supports multiple images.
.TP
.B summarize, sum
Create concise summaries of text with customizable styles.
.TP
.B completion
Generate shell completions for bash, elvish, fish, powershell, and zsh.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
These options must be placed BEFORE the subcommand:
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-model " " \fIMODEL\fR
Select model preset (default: llama3.1). See MODELS section.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prompt " " \fIMODE\fR
Set system prompt mode: default, tool_user, code, code_with_tools.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-think
Enable think mode for models that support reasoning.
.TP
.BR \-\-plain
Output plain text without markdown formatting.
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Dry-run mode: print configuration and exit without executing.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Quiet mode: only errors and the final answer (no spinner, no tool calls).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity: \-v (verbose), \-vv (trace).
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List available models and prompt modes, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-tools
Force enable tools even if model doesn't advertise support.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-code
Code mode: optimize response for code output.
.TP
.BR \-\-ignore\-agents
Ignore AGENTS.md file in current directory (disable context injection).
.TP
.BR \-\-soulless
Skip SOUL.md personality (use neutral personality).
.TP
.BR \-\-init\-config
Initialize/create sample configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-\-db " " \fIPATH\fR
Custom database path (overrides default ~/.local/share/sprachspiel/sprachspiel.db).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.SH CHAT OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-anonymous
Start anonymous session (no history persistence).
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-load " " \fISESSION\fR
Load a named session.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-model " " \fIMODEL\fR
Model preset to use.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-think
Enable think mode for models that support it.
.TP
.BR \-\-tools
Force enable tools even if model doesn't advertise support.
.TP
.BR \-\-tools\-output " " \fILEVEL\fR
Tool output verbosity: compact, full, hidden (default: compact).
.TP
.BR \-\-ignore\-agents
Ignore AGENTS.md file in current directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-soulless
Skip SOUL.md personality (use neutral personality).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity: \-v (verbose), \-vv (trace).
.PP
Interactive commands available inside chat:
.in +4
/quit, /exit \- Exit chat session
.br
/new \- Start a new conversation (previous messages remain searchable)
.br
/forget [--yes] \- Delete conversation completely and start fresh (requires --yes)
.br
/help \- Show available commands
.br
/model <name> \- Switch model mid-session
.br
/system <prompt> \- Change system prompt
.br
/think [on|off] \- Toggle, enable, or disable think mode
.br
/tools \- Toggle tools
.br
/toggle-style \- Toggle style rendering (Mermaid diagrams, syntax highlighting, table format)
.br
/tools-output <level> \- Set tool output level (compact|full|hidden)
.br
/compact \- Compact conversation history
.br
/retry \- Regenerate last response
.br
/undo \- Undo last message (remove response, show last input)
.br
/save [name] \- Save current session
.br
/load <name> \- Load a saved session
.br
/export <format> [file] \- Export conversation (md, json)
.br
/list \- List saved sessions for this project
.br
/info \- Show current session information
.br
/context \- Show context metrics, token usage, and decay statistics
.br
/search <query> \- Search conversation history (semantic search)
.br
/reindex [--yes] \- Regenerate embeddings for all content (requires --yes)
.br
/retrieval \- Toggle semantic retrieval from conversation history
.br
/fact add <text> [--global] \- Add a fact (project scope by default)
.br
/fact list [--global] \- List stored facts
.br
/fact search <query> \- Search stored facts
.br
/fact remove <id> \- Remove a fact by ID
.br
/fact prune \- Prune old facts using decay cycle
.br
/note add <content> [--title <title>] [--global] \- Add a note
.br
/note list [--global] \- List stored notes
.br
/note show <id> \- Show a note by ID
.br
/note edit <id> [--title <title>] [--content <content>] \- Edit a note
.br
/note delete <id> \- Delete a note by ID
.br
/note search <query> [--global] [limit] \- Search stored notes
.br
/doc import <path> [--global] \- Import a document (TXT, MD, ORG only)
.br
/doc list [--global] \- List imported documents
.br
/doc show <id> \- Show document content (rendered as markdown)
.br
/doc delete <id> \- Delete a document by ID
.br
/feedback good|bad|correction:<text> [msg:id] \- Submit feedback on assistant response
.br
/content prune \- Manually trigger content decay cycle
.br
/skill \- List available skills
.br
/skill <name> \- Activate a skill for this session
.br
/ocr <file> [mode] \- Extract text from image (modes: text, table, figure, formula)
.br
/vision <path> [prompt] \- Analyze image with vision model
.br
/translate <src:dst> <text> \- Translate text between languages
.br
/summarize <text> \- Summarize text
.br
/todo add <desc> \- Add a todo
.br
/todo list \- List todos
.br
/todo done <id> \- Mark todo as done
.br
/todo get <id> \- Get a todo by ID
.br
/todo edit <id> [options] \- Edit a todo (title, description, priority)
.br
/todo update <id> [options] \- Update a todo (status, priority)
.br
/todo delete <id> \- Delete a todo
.br
/todo clear-done \- Clear completed todos
.br
/todo clear-all \- Clear all todos
.in -4
.PP
Tab completion available for commands and model names.
.br
Prompt shows active modes in the status bar: 🧠 for think, 🔧 for tools, 🎨 for style enabled (📄 for style disabled).
.br
Visual indicators show tool activity in DIM gray (hidden in quiet mode):
.br
.in +4
\fB🔧\fR tool call (always visible in Normal+ mode)
.br
\fB📖\fR skill loaded
.br
\fB📄\fR document imported
.br
\fB📝\fR note created/updated
.br
\fB🗑️\fR note deleted
.br
\fB👍\fR/\fB👎\fR/\fB✎\fR feedback submitted
.br
\fB💾\fR/\fB⏭\fR fact stored/skipped
.br
\fB⚡\fR command executing
.in -4
.br
Skills are loaded proactively — the LLM calls skill_view() when it detects
a task matching a skill's description (PDF processing, OCR, code analysis, etc.).
.br
Session storage: ~/.local/share/sprachspiel/conversations/<project-id>/default.json
.br
Project ID is derived from git remote URL or folder name.
.SH LOGGING
Logs are written to both stderr and a log file:
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/sprachspiel/sprachspiel.log
Default log file (always warn level and above).
.PP
Log rotation: when the file exceeds 5 MB, it is renamed to
.IR sprachspiel.log.1
and a new file is created.
.PP
PII audit: sensitive data (API keys, tokens, personal identifiers) is automatically truncated in log output.
.PP
Verbosity levels:
.in +4
\fBQuiet\fR (\-q): errors only
.br
\fBNormal\fR (default): warnings + errors
.br
\fBVerbose\fR (\-v): debug + warnings + errors
.br
\fBTrace\fR (\-vv): all internals including embedding and token budgets
.in -4
.PP
Terminal output uses colored log levels; file output uses plain timestamps.
.SH TRANSLATE OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-model " " \fIMODEL\fR
Model preset to use (default: translategemma).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prompt " " \fISTYLE\fR
Translation style: formal, casual, technical, literary.
.TP
.BR \-\-list " [" \fIFILTER\fR "]"
List supported languages, optionally filter by substring.
.TP
.B LANGUAGE
Language pair in format [source:]target (e.g., en:pt, :pt for auto-detect).
.SH OCR OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " " \fIMODE\fR
Extraction mode: text (default), table, figure, formula.
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Output as JSON (one object per line for batch).
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-tokens " " \fINUM\fR
Maximum tokens per image (default: 8192).
.TP
.B FILE
One or more image files: PNG, JPG, JPEG, WebP, GIF.
.SH VISION OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-model " " \fIMODEL\fR
Model preset to use (default: moondream).
.TP
.BR \-\-detailed
Request detailed image analysis.
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Output as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-tokens " " \fINUM\fR
Maximum tokens for response (default: 4096).
.TP
.B FILE
One or more image files: PNG, JPG, JPEG, WebP, GIF.
.SH SUMMARIZE OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-max\-length " " \fIWORDS\fR
Maximum summary length in words (default: 300).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format: paragraph, bullets, both (default).
.TP
.BR \-\-style " " \fISTYLE\fR
Focus style: general (default), technical, academic, business.
.SH COMPLETION OPTIONS
.TP
.B SHELL
Shell to generate completions for: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh.
.SH MODELS
Built-in model presets (always available):
.PP
.TS
tab(|);
l l l l.
Preset|Model|Context|Best For
_
llama3.1|llama3.1:8b|4K|General queries (default)
translategemma|translategemma:4b|4K|Translation
glm-ocr|glm-ocr:bf16|Auto|OCR/image extraction
moondream|moondream:1.8b|8K|Vision/image analysis
.TE
.PP
Run 'sprach --list' to see all available models including user-defined ones.
.SH EXAMPLES
Basic query:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sprach "What is Rust?"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Use specific model:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sprach -m qwen3 query "Explain quantum computing"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Enable think mode:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sprach -t query "Solve this step by step"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Code mode (for programming):
.PP
.nf
.RS
sprach -c query "Write a Rust function"
sprach -c -m qwen3-coder query "Implement a thread pool"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Translate text:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sprach translate en:pt "Hello world"
sprach translate :pt "Auto-detect source"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Extract text from image (OCR):
.PP
.nf
.RS
sprach ocr document.png
sprach ocr --mode table spreadsheet.png
.RE
.fi
.PP
Analyze image (Vision):
.PP
.nf
.RS
sprach vision photo.jpg
sprach vision --detailed landscape.png
sprach vision -m llava image1.png image2.png
.RE
.fi
.PP
Summarize text:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sprach summarize "Long text here..."
sprach summarize --style technical "Long text"
echo "Long text" | sprach summarize --style technical
.RE
.fi
.PP
Debug mode (verbose logging):
.PP
.nf
.RS
sprach -v query "Test query"
sprach -v -m llama3.1 query "Verbose with specific model"
sprach -vv query "Trace level logging"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Pipe from stdin:
.PP
.nf
.RS
cat file.txt | sprach summarize
cat article.pdf | pdftotext - - | sprach summarize
.RE
.fi
.PP
Use project context from AGENTS.md:
.PP
.nf
.RS
# With AGENTS.md in current directory
sprach "Explain the project structure"
sprach "How do I run the tests?"

# Ignore AGENTS.md for general queries
sprach --ignore-agents "What is machine learning?"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Chain commands:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sprach ocr document.png | sprach summarize
sprach ocr japanese.png | sprach translate ja:pt
sprach vision photo.jpg | sprach summarize
.RE
.fi
.PP
Interactive chat:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sprach chat
sprach chat -a  # anonymous mode
sprach chat -m qwen3.5 --tools
.RE
.fi
.PP
List available models:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sprach --list
.RE
.fi
.PP
Generate shell completions:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sprach completion bash > ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/sprach
sprach completion zsh > ~/.zfunc/_sprach
.RE
.fi
.SH LANGUAGE CODES
Supported translation language codes include:
.PP
pt, pt-BR (br, brazil), en (english), es (spanish), fr (french), de (german),
it (italian), ja (japanese), zh-Hans (zh-cn), zh-Hant (zh-tw), he (hebrew),
ko (korean), ru (russian), ar (arabic), hi (hindi), and 40+ more.
.PP
Use \fBsprach translate --list\fR to see all supported languages.
.SH PROMPT MODES
.TP
.B default
General purpose queries with markdown formatting.
.TP
.B tool_user
Enhanced prompt for tool usage (Pokemon, Weather, Web Search).
.TP
.B code
Code-focused responses, minimal explanations.
.TP
.B code_with_tools
Code mode with web search tools enabled.
.TP
.B summarize
Professional summarization guidelines.
.TP
.B pepe
Sarcastic personality (activated for pepe model).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OLLAMA_HOST
Override the default LLM server host (default: localhost:11434).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sprachspiel/config.toml
User configuration file (model presets, tool settings, output preferences).
Supports per-subcommand configuration: [model.query], [model.chat], [model.summarize], [model.code], [model.vision].
Each subcommand can override model, thinking, and tools from global [model] settings.
Thinking mode priority: CLI flags > subcommand config > global config > model default > hardcoded default.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sprachspiel/models.toml
User-defined model configurations. Add custom models or override built-in parameters.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sprachspiel/SOUL.md
User-defined agent personality. Defines identity, behavior, and limits. Falls back to PERSONALITY_DEFAULT when missing. Use --soulless to skip.
.TP
.I ./AGENTS.md
Project context file automatically loaded when present in current directory. Provides project-specific instructions and context to the model. Can be disabled with --ignore-agents flag.
.TP
.I src/config.rs
Built-in model configurations (llama3.1, translategemma, glm-ocr, moondream).
.TP
.I src/prompts.rs
System prompt definitions.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments or usage.
.TP
.B 3
Model error or server connection failure.
